// UnusedExportCheck — E3092 / E3093 / E3094: a declaration more widely visible than its uses require.
//
// Three diagnostics, one walk (`specs/unused-export.md`):
//   • E3092 `semanticUnusedExportedSymbol`  — an `export` decl no file outside its declaring one names
//   • E3093 `semanticExportableAsModule`    — an `export` decl named only inside its declaring subtree
//   • E3094 `semanticUnusedModuleSymbol`    — a `module` decl no file outside its declaring one names
//
// ⭐⭐ **`public` IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS PASS EXISTS AT ALL, AND IT IS WHY THERE IS NO STDLIB
// CARVE-OUT HERE.** Without it the audit conflates two things: `export` states VISIBILITY, and reading it
// as a claim about USE condemns a shared module's surface that this particular program does not happen to
// call. `public` separates them:
//   • `export` — other files may see this, AND I expect this program to use it. Audited here.
//   • `public` — this is API surface. Exempt, because "no caller in THIS compilation" is not "dead".
//
// ⇒ **THIS PASS NEEDS NO STDLIB EXEMPTION.** Every exported declaration under `stdlib/` is `public`, so
// they fall out at the `isProgramWideTier`-and-not-`global` test below like any other author's API
// surface would. Without that, the pass would emit E3092 against every stdlib typealias the user
// happens not to mention — an exemption by PATH is what a library that is not `public` would force.
//
// ⚠ **THE PASS DOES KNOW ABOUT THE LIBRARY IN ONE PLACE, AND IT IS THE READER SIDE** — `noteRead`
// refuses to let a library file be credited with a reference to an AUTHOR's declaration, because a
// monomorphized `Array with Item` body carries `stdlib/Array.maxon` as its source file and cannot
// possibly have named `Item`. The rule and what it cost are stated in full there.
//
// ⛔ **THE RUNTIME TIER IS EXEMPT BY PATH.** The argument above turns on every exported `stdlib/`
// declaration being `public`; a `runtime/` declaration is not, so an `export`ed one would be audited like
// an author's. It cannot be: every runtime declaration is permanently "unused" to this pass by
// construction, because a runtime entry is reached by the COMPILER looking up a NAME, never by a source
// file referencing it. There is no program in which one of them acquires a reader, so E3092/E3093/E3094
// over that tier report nothing a change could ever fix. Keyed on `isRuntimeSourceFile` so it fails
// CLOSED: a file outside `runtime/` is audited.
//
// ⛔ **THE SECOND EXEMPTION IS A SIGNATURE DEMAND, AND IT IS PER DECLARATION RATHER THAN BY PATH** — see
// `reachedSignatureDemands`. A type that E3167 requires an exported or `module` function to be able to
// name is credited at the tier E3167 judges that function at, so this pass and E3167 cannot contradict each other on one
// program.
//
// ⚠ **WHAT IS STILL AUDITED IN `stdlib/`: its `module` declarations** (all in `String.maxon`).
// That is deliberate — `module` is the marked, narrower tier there, and E3094 is exactly the signal its
// author wants if a door stops being reached. Each of them is named from outside `String.maxon`, so none
// fires.

// ── Gates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ⭐ **THE STRUCTURAL GATE IS THE PIPELINE'S, NOT THIS PASS'S.** A half-resolved reader would produce
// spurious findings, and the schedule already rules that out: `PassPipeline.run` throws the moment ANY
// pass reports a diagnostic, and this pass is scheduled after `semanticCheck`, so reaching it means the
// project's diagnostic list is empty. Re-testing it here would be a second answer to a question the
// driver has already answered.

// ── What is seeded ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Which namespace a tracked declaration lives in. A reference names a FUNCTION, a TYPE or a top-level
// BINDING, and the three cannot be confused for one another at a use site, so they are keyed apart.
enum TrackedDeclKind
	trackedFunction
	trackedType
	trackedBinding
end 'TrackedDeclKind'

// One `export`/`module` declaration and the widest scope anything has been seen to read it from.
//
// ⚠ **THE TWO BITS ARE MONOTONIC AND ARE NEVER NARROWED.** A declaration read from two files is read
// from the wider of them, so every `note` widens or does nothing; a `set` that could clear one would make
// the answer depend on which reader was visited last.
type TrackedDecl
	export var kind as TrackedDeclKind

	// The key a reference is matched against — a function's compiled name, a type's name, or a binding's
	// name. NOT the display spelling: `displayName` is what the message prints.
	export var key as ByteArray
	export var displayName as String

	// The word the message calls this declaration: "function", "type", "typealias", "constant", "variable".
	// The spec expectations quote it verbatim, so the spelling is pinned.
	export var noun as String
	export var visibility as Visibility
	export var declFile as AuditedFile
	export var nameLine as LineNumber
	export var nameColumn as ColumnNumber
	export var sawOutsideFile as bool
	export var sawOutsideModule as bool

	static function create(kind TrackedDeclKind, key ByteArray, displayName String, noun String, visibility Visibility, declFile AuditedFile, nameLine LineNumber, nameColumn ColumnNumber) returns TrackedDecl
		return Self{kind: kind, key: key, displayName: displayName, noun: noun, visibility: visibility, declFile: declFile, nameLine: nameLine, nameColumn: nameColumn, sawOutsideFile: false, sawOutsideModule: false}
	end 'create'
end 'TrackedDecl'

typealias TrackedDeclArray = Array with TrackedDecl
typealias TrackedDeclIndex = int(0 to u64.max)

// ⛔⛔ **A BARE NAME IS NOT A DECLARATION'S IDENTITY, AND KEYING THIS BY ONE PANICKED.** Two files in
// DIFFERENT DIRECTORIES may each declare `type NsDeep` or `function pick` — that is what a namespace is
// FOR, and `specs/namespace-qualified-resolution.md` is thirty cases about it. The index was a
// `Map with (ByteArray, TrackedDeclIndex)`, so the second declaration's `insert` threw `keyAlreadyExists`
// and the pass aborted the compile: MEASURED by `scale-test`'s generated corpus, which emits a namespace
// ladder — and NOT by any of the 6,377 spec cases, because none of them declares a contested name in a
// program that also compiles clean.
//
// ⇒ One name maps to EVERY declaration wearing it, and a reference to that name credits all of them.
// That OVER-approximates where two namespaces contest a name — a use of `alpha.pick` also credits
// `beta.pick` — and the direction is deliberate: crediting a reference too widely can only SUPPRESS a
// finding, while resolving to the wrong one of two claimants would report a live declaration as dead.
// Telling them apart needs the reader's own namespace precedence, which is `ProgramSignatures`' answer to
// give, not this pass's to re-derive.
typealias TrackedDeclIndexArray = Array with TrackedDeclIndex
typealias TrackedDeclIndexMap = Map with (ByteArray, TrackedDeclIndexArray)

// ⭐⭐ **EVERY STORED GLOBAL'S `.data` LABEL, MAPPED TO THE DECLARATION THAT OWNS IT.** A `globalAddr`
// op carries the LABEL and this seed is keyed by source NAME, so somewhere the two have to be joined —
// `noteGlobalLabel` is the one place that asks.
//
// ⚠⚠ **IT IS A MAP BECAUSE THE JOIN WAS A SCAN OF THE WHOLE DECLARATION ARENA AT EVERY `globalAddr`
// OP, AND THAT PRODUCT WAS THIS PASS'S SUPERLINEAR TERM.** Both of its factors DOUBLE per rung of the
// scaling ladder — the top-level `let`/`var` COUNT and the number of sites that read one — so the scan
// quadrupled while everything around it doubled. MEASURED, `phase:checkUnusedExports` CPU per doubling:
// x1.43 x1.58 x1.86 x2.28 x2.74, monotonic, against x2.00 for linear.
//
// ⛔ **AND THE MEMORY COLUMNS READ IT AS PERFECTLY LINEAR — x1.90 allocations, x1.89 bytes — because a
// scan step ALLOCATES NOTHING.** It copies a `TopLevelDecl`, which RETAINS six managed handles (its
// whole `TokenArray` among them) and releases them again, so the entire quadratic was refcount traffic.
// That is the class the CPU column was added to catch, and no other column of the instrument could see it.
typealias GlobalLabelIndexMap = Map with (ByteArray, TopLevelDeclIndex)

// The type names each reader file has already been credited with, one key per `(reader, name)` pair. What a
// transitive walk credits is a function of the name and the READER alone, and a credit only ever widens, so
// a name a reader was credited with once needs no second walk from that reader — and a self-referential type
// terminates. Keyed per reader, never pass-wide: a second reader must not inherit the first one's credits.
typealias CreditedTypeNameId = int(0 to u32.max)
typealias CreditedTypeNameKey = int(0 to u64.max)
typealias CreditedTypeNameKeySet = Set with CreditedTypeNameKey
typealias CreditedTypeNameIdMap = Map with (ByteArray, CreditedTypeNameId)

let AuditedFileKeyShift = 32 as CreditedTypeNameKey

// A source file a declaration lives in or a reference is read from, with what every credit asks about it
// answered once. One per `FilePath.toString()` spelling, so equal indexes mean equal spellings — which is
// the same-file test `noteRead` needs and the one it made by comparing those two strings.
typealias AuditedFileIndex = int(0 to u32.max)

type AuditedFile
	export let index as AuditedFileIndex
	export let path as FilePath
	export let pathText as String
	export let moduleDirectory as String
	export let isLibrary as bool

	static function create(index AuditedFileIndex, path FilePath, pathText String, moduleDirectory String, isLibrary bool) returns AuditedFile
		return Self{index: index, path: path, pathText: pathText, moduleDirectory: moduleDirectory, isLibrary: isLibrary}
	end 'create'
end 'AuditedFile'

typealias AuditedFileMap = Map with (String, AuditedFile)

// The LIBRARY's source files, keyed by the `FilePath.toString()` spelling. A SET and not a second walk,
// because `isStdlibSourceFile` is a memo probe on a `FilePath` key — which clones and lower-cases the path —
// while this is asked of every reader and every declaration, and a String key hashes in place.
typealias LibrarySourcePathSet = Set with String

typealias EntryPointNameSet = Set with ByteArray

// The author's files, the library's, and the runtime tier's, told apart in ONE walk over
// `project.db.sourcePaths`. All three come from the same pair of answers per path, so the populations
// cannot come to disagree about a file the way independently-filtered walks could. `runtimeFiles` is a
// SUBSET of `libraryFiles`: a runtime file is the library's for `noteRead`'s rule and additionally
// exempt from emission.
type SourcePathSplit
	export let userFiles as FilePathArray
	export let libraryFiles as LibrarySourcePathSet
	export let runtimeFiles as LibrarySourcePathSet

	static function create(userFiles FilePathArray, libraryFiles LibrarySourcePathSet, runtimeFiles LibrarySourcePathSet) returns SourcePathSplit
		return Self{userFiles: userFiles, libraryFiles: libraryFiles, runtimeFiles: runtimeFiles}
	end 'create'
end 'SourcePathSplit'

// The seed, plus the three by-name indexes a reference is resolved through. One array so emission order
// is DECLARATION order and therefore deterministic — a map iteration would make the diagnostic order an
// artifact of hashing, and two runs of one compiler must print the same bytes.
type TrackedDecls
	export var entries as TrackedDeclArray
	export var functionIndex as TrackedDeclIndexMap
	export var typeIndex as TrackedDeclIndexMap
	export var bindingIndex as TrackedDeclIndexMap

	// Which files are the library's, for `noteRead`'s rule: a property of the PROGRAM rather than of any one
	// credit, so it rides here instead of being threaded through every `note*`.
	export let libraryFiles as LibrarySourcePathSet

	// The fourth index, and the only one keyed by something other than a source name — see
	// `GlobalLabelIndexMap`. It rides here for `libraryFiles`' reason.
	export let globalLabels as GlobalLabelIndexMap

	var files as AuditedFileMap
	var creditedTypeNameIds as CreditedTypeNameIdMap
	var creditedTypeNames as CreditedTypeNameKeySet

	static function create(libraryFiles LibrarySourcePathSet, globalLabels GlobalLabelIndexMap) returns TrackedDecls
		return Self{entries: TrackedDeclArray.create(), functionIndex: TrackedDeclIndexMap.create(), typeIndex: TrackedDeclIndexMap.create(), bindingIndex: TrackedDeclIndexMap.create(), libraryFiles: libraryFiles, globalLabels: globalLabels, files: AuditedFileMap.create(), creditedTypeNameIds: CreditedTypeNameIdMap.create(), creditedTypeNames: CreditedTypeNameKeySet.create()}
	end 'create'

	function fileOf(path FilePath, signatures ProgramSignatures) returns AuditedFile
		let pathText = path.toString()

		if let known = try self.files.get(pathText) 'known'
			return known
		end 'known'

		let file = AuditedFile.create(self.files.count() as AuditedFileIndex, path: path, pathText: pathText, moduleDirectory: signatures.moduleDirectoryOf(path), isLibrary: self.libraryFiles.contains(pathText))
		self.files.upsert(pathText, value: file)
		return file
	end 'fileOf'

	// Whether `reader` is credited with `name` for the first time — see `CreditedTypeNameKey`.
	function creditsTypeNameFirst(name ByteArray, reader AuditedFile) returns bool
		var nameId = self.creditedTypeNameIds.count() as CreditedTypeNameId

		if let known = try self.creditedTypeNameIds.get(name) 'known'
			nameId = known
		end 'known' else 'unseen'
			self.creditedTypeNameIds.upsert(name, value: nameId)
		end 'unseen'

		let key = ((reader.index as CreditedTypeNameKey) shl AuditedFileKeyShift) or (nameId as CreditedTypeNameKey)

		if self.creditedTypeNames.contains(key) 'alreadyCredited'
			return false
		end 'alreadyCredited'

		self.creditedTypeNames.insert(key)
		return true
	end 'creditsTypeNameFirst'

	function add(decl TrackedDecl)
		let at = self.entries.count()
		self.entries.push(decl)

		match decl.kind 'kind'
			trackedFunction then self.indexUnder(self.functionIndex, key: decl.key, at: at)
			trackedType then self.indexUnder(self.typeIndex, key: decl.key, at: at)
			trackedBinding then self.indexUnder(self.bindingIndex, key: decl.key, at: at)
		end 'kind'
	end 'add'

	// `upsert`, not `insert`: a contested bare name is a legal program, not a collision — see
	// `TrackedDeclIndexMap`.
	// ⚠ The existing list is COPIED out before the write rather than pushed to in place: `get` hands back a
	// borrow of the map's own slot, and mutating the map through `upsert` while that borrow is live is
	// E3070. Built fresh, the borrow ends at the `if`.
	function indexUnder(index TrackedDeclIndexMap, key ByteArray, at TrackedDeclIndex)
		var claimants = TrackedDeclIndexArray.create()

		if let existing = try index.get(key) 'alreadyClaimed'
			claimants.append(existing)
		end 'alreadyClaimed'

		claimants.push(at)
		index.upsert(key, value: claimants)
	end 'indexUnder'

	function at(index TrackedDeclIndex) returns TrackedDecl
		return try self.entries.get(index) otherwise panic("TrackedDecls.at: OOB at {index} — every index handed out is one this seed minted")
	end 'at'
end 'TrackedDecls'

// ── The pass ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

module function checkUnusedExports(project Project, module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures) throws CompileError
	let sources = try splitSourcePaths(project)

	let entryPoints = try entryPointNamesOf(project, userFiles: sources.userFiles)

	var tracked = TrackedDecls.create(sources.libraryFiles, globalLabels: indexGlobalLabels(signatures))
	seedFunctions(module, signatures: signatures, entryPoints: entryPoints, tracked: tracked)
	try seedTypes(project, signatures: signatures, userFiles: sources.userFiles, tracked: tracked)
	seedBindings(signatures, tracked: tracked)

	if tracked.entries.count() == 0 'nothingWiderThanAFile'
		return
	end 'nothingWiderThanAFile'

	collectReferences(module, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, moduleTypeNames: project.typeNames)
	try collectFileTypeReferences(project, signatures: signatures, userFiles: sources.userFiles, tracked: tracked)
	emitDiagnostics(project, tracked: tracked, runtimeFiles: sources.runtimeFiles, demanded: reachedSignatureDemands(project, tracked: tracked))
end 'checkUnusedExports'

function splitSourcePaths(project Project) returns SourcePathSplit throws CompileError
	var paths = FilePathArray.create()
	var libraryFiles = LibrarySourcePathSet.create()
	var runtimeFiles = LibrarySourcePathSet.create()

	for path in project.db.sourcePaths 'eachFile'
		if isStdlibSourceFile(project, path: path) 'stdlibFile'
			libraryFiles.insert(path.toString())
			continue
		end 'stdlibFile'

		if isRuntimeSourceFile(project, path: path) 'runtimeFile'
			libraryFiles.insert(path.toString())
			runtimeFiles.insert(path.toString())
			continue
		end 'runtimeFile'

		paths.push(path)
	end 'eachFile'

	return SourcePathSplit.create(paths, libraryFiles: libraryFiles, runtimeFiles: runtimeFiles)
end 'splitSourcePaths'

// One pass over the declaration arena, so `noteGlobalLabel` is a lookup and not a scan of it.
//
// ⚠ **FIRST WINS, exactly as the scan's `return` did.** Two declarations cannot share a `.data` label
// — it is minted from the storage key, which is what makes featA's `counter` and featB's `counter` two
// slots — but the tie is broken here anyway, so the answer can never come to depend on which of two
// claimants a map happened to keep.
function indexGlobalLabels(signatures ProgramSignatures) returns GlobalLabelIndexMap
	var labels = GlobalLabelIndexMap.create()

	for i in 0 upto signatures.topLevelDeclCount() 'eachDecl'
		let decl = signatures.declAt(i)

		// An immutable binding is INLINED at its use and has no slot to take the address of, so it has no
		// label at all — see `TopLevelDecl.dataLabel`.
		if not decl.hasStorage or labels.contains(decl.dataLabel) 'noSlotOrAlreadyClaimed'
			continue
		end 'noSlotOrAlreadyClaimed'

		labels.upsert(decl.dataLabel, value: i)
	end 'eachDecl'

	return labels
end 'indexGlobalLabels'

// ── Seeding ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Is this tier one the audit has anything to say about? `file` is already as narrow as a declaration
// gets, and `public` is the author's statement that "nobody here calls it" is not a finding.
function tierIsAudited(visibility Visibility) returns bool
	return match visibility 'tier'
		file gives false
		public gives false
		module gives true
		global gives true
	end 'tier'
end 'tierIsAudited'

// ⭐ **THE NAMES NO SOURCE LINE DECLARES.** A synthesized helper has no `export` an author could drop, so
// a finding about one is a finding about the compiler.
module function isSynthesizedName(name ByteArray) returns bool
	let text = String.from(name)
	return text.startsWith("__") or text.contains("$closure_") or text.contains(".unionCases")
end 'isSynthesizedName'

// The functions nothing in the source calls. The entry is `Project.entryFunctionName` rather than
// the literal `main`: a `main` that another entry has displaced needs a caller like any other
// export. Every target of a `.maxproj` and every task of a `.maxtasks` counts, not only the one
// this build enters at: the driver compiles the file with one of them as the entry and reaches the
// others by name. They are read through the driver's own `taskNamesIn`, so the two cannot disagree
// on what one is.
function entryPointNamesOf(project Project, userFiles FilePathArray) returns EntryPointNameSet throws CompileError
	var names = EntryPointNameSet.create()
	names.insert(project.entryFunctionName)

	for path in userFiles 'eachFile'
		if not isDriverFileName(path.filename()) 'notADriverFile'
			continue
		end 'notADriverFile'

		let entry = try sourceEntryOf(project, path: path)
		let declared = try taskNamesIn(entry.content) otherwise continue

		for task in declared 'eachTask'
			names.insert(task.toByteArray())
		end 'eachTask'
	end 'eachFile'

	return names
end 'entryPointNamesOf'

function seedFunctions(module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures, entryPoints EntryPointNameSet, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for func in module.functions 'eachFunc'
		if not tierIsAudited(func.visibility) 'narrowEnoughAlready'
			continue
		end 'narrowEnoughAlready'

		if func.sourceFilePath.toString().isEmpty() 'synthesizedFunction'
			continue
		end 'synthesizedFunction'

		if isSynthesizedName(func.name) or entryPoints.contains(func.name) 'noSourceLevelCaller'
			continue
		end 'noSourceLevelCaller'

		// ⭐ **A METHOD TAKES ITS TIER FROM ITS DECLARING TYPE, SO THE TYPE OWNS THE DIAGNOSTIC.** Auditing
		// `Point.sum` on its own reports an internal helper of a public type as dead, and — worse — an
		// un-`export`ed method of a `module` type would report as E3093, advising a narrowing that is not
		// expressible. `specs/unused-export.md`'s `error.unused-exported-type` PINS it: `LocalPoint`
		// declares two exported methods and the case expects exactly ONE diagnostic, about the type.
		if namesAMethodOnATrackedType(signatures, qualifiedName: func.name) 'theTypeOwnsIt'
			continue
		end 'theTypeOwnsIt'

		// ⭐ **THE MESSAGE SPELLS A FUNCTION WITH ITS NAMESPACE, AND THE SPELLING IS ASKED FOR RATHER THAN
		// BUILT.** `specs/unused-export.md` expects `'api.unusedHelper'`, not the bare registration name the
		// IR carries. `diagnosticCalleeSpelling` is the door every other visibility diagnostic already
		// spells a callee through — including the guard against re-qualifying a name that is already
		// qualified (`alpha.alpha.pick`), which a second copy of the join here would have got wrong.
		tracked.add(TrackedDecl.create(TrackedDeclKind.trackedFunction, key: func.name, displayName: String.from(signatures.diagnosticCalleeSpelling(func.name)), noun: "function", visibility: func.visibility, declFile: tracked.fileOf(func.sourceFilePath, signatures: signatures), nameLine: func.nameLine, nameColumn: func.nameColumn))
	end 'eachFunc'
end 'seedFunctions'

// `Owner.method` where `Owner` is a declared struct or enum. The owner is split off the LAST dot, so a
// namespace-qualified free function (`api.helper`) is only a method if `api` is itself a type name.
function namesAMethodOnATrackedType(signatures ProgramSignatures, qualifiedName ByteArray) returns bool
	return match splitQualifiedName(qualifiedName) 'split'
		notQualified gives false
		parts(owner, _) gives signatures.containsStructInAnyFile(owner) or signatures.containsEnumInAnyFile(owner)
	end 'split'
end 'namesAMethodOnATrackedType'

// ⭐ **TYPES ARE SEEDED FROM THE PARSE ARTIFACTS, NOT FROM THE LAYOUT REGISTRIES, BECAUSE THE POSITION
// LIVES THERE.** `StructLayout` and `EnumLayout` carry a `declFilePath` and no name position, and that is
// a DELIBERATE design this pass must not undo: `TypeNameDecl`'s own header records why one array in source
// order beats a position added to each of the four layout types (which of a file's `type Box` and
// `typealias Box` came second is a fact no single registry holds). So the walk is per file, in source
// order, and the tier is looked up per name.
function seedTypes(project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, userFiles FilePathArray, tracked TrackedDecls) throws CompileError
	for path in userFiles 'eachFile'
		let artifact = try queryParseOps(project, path: path)

		for decl in artifact.typeNameDecls 'eachTypeName'
			seedOneTypeName(signatures, decl: decl, tracked: tracked)
		end 'eachTypeName'
	end 'eachFile'
end 'seedTypes'

function seedOneTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, decl TypeNameDecl, tracked TrackedDecls)
	if isSynthesizedName(decl.name) 'compilerOwned'
		return
	end 'compilerOwned'

	let visibility = declaredTypeVisibility(signatures, decl: decl)

	if not tierIsAudited(visibility) 'narrowEnoughAlready'
		return
	end 'narrowEnoughAlready'

	tracked.add(TrackedDecl.create(TrackedDeclKind.trackedType, key: decl.name, displayName: String.from(decl.name), noun: typeDeclNoun(decl.claim.kind), visibility: visibility, declFile: tracked.fileOf(decl.claim.declFilePath, signatures: signatures), nameLine: decl.nameLine, nameColumn: decl.nameColumn))
end 'seedOneTypeName'

// ⭐ **WHICH TIERS THIS AUDIT TRACKS — and it is deliberately NOT the same question as "what tier was
// this declared at".** A kind this audit does not cover answers `file`, which the caller reads as
// "nothing to audit"; that is the honest answer for a kind whose unused-export rule has never been
// written, not a sentinel and not a claim about the source.
//
// ⚠ **SO IT MAY NOT BE REPLACED WHOLESALE BY `decl.claim.visibility`**, which is the EFFECTIVE tier for
// every kind (see `TypeNameClaim.visibility`). The one arm where the two ask the same question is the
// ranged alias, and that arm now reads the claim rather than re-deriving it through `aliasOf` — the two
// answered identically by construction (own-file lookup returns this very declaration), which is exactly
// what made the second derivation a copy rather than a check.
function declaredTypeVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, decl TypeNameDecl) returns Visibility
	match decl.claim.kind 'kind'
		structType then return declaredStructVisibility(signatures, name: decl.name, declFilePath: decl.claim.declFilePath)
		enumType then return declaredEnumVisibility(signatures, name: decl.name, declFilePath: decl.claim.declFilePath)
		unionType then return declaredEnumVisibility(signatures, name: decl.name, declFilePath: decl.claim.declFilePath)
		interfaceType then return Visibility.file
		rangedAlias then return decl.claim.visibility
		functionAlias then return Visibility.file
		genericAlias then return Visibility.file
		tupleAlias then return Visibility.file
	end 'kind'
end 'declaredTypeVisibility'

function declaredStructVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, name ByteArray, declFilePath FilePath) returns Visibility
	return match signatures.structFor(name, readerFilePath: declFilePath) 'lookup'
		declared(layout) gives layout.visibility
		undeclared gives Visibility.file
	end 'lookup'
end 'declaredStructVisibility'

function declaredEnumVisibility(signatures ProgramSignatures, name ByteArray, declFilePath FilePath) returns Visibility
	return match signatures.enumFor(name, readerFilePath: declFilePath) 'lookup'
		declared(layout) gives layout.visibility
		undeclared gives Visibility.file
	end 'lookup'
end 'declaredEnumVisibility'

// The word the diagnostic calls a type declaration: a struct, enum or union is a "type" and an alias
// is a "typealias".
function typeDeclNoun(kind TypeDeclKind) returns String
	return match kind 'kind'
		structType gives "type"
		enumType gives "type"
		unionType gives "type"
		interfaceType gives "type"
		rangedAlias gives "typealias"
		functionAlias gives "typealias"
		genericAlias gives "typealias"
		tupleAlias gives "typealias"
	end 'kind'
end 'typeDeclNoun'

function seedBindings(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.topLevelDeclCount() 'eachDecl'
		let decl = signatures.declAt(i)

		if not tierIsAudited(decl.visibility) 'narrowEnoughAlready'
			continue
		end 'narrowEnoughAlready'

		if isSynthesizedName(decl.name) 'compilerOwned'
			continue
		end 'compilerOwned'

		tracked.add(TrackedDecl.create(TrackedDeclKind.trackedBinding, key: decl.name, displayName: String.from(decl.name), noun: "variable" if decl.mutable else "constant", visibility: decl.visibility, declFile: tracked.fileOf(decl.declFilePath, signatures: signatures), nameLine: decl.nameLine, nameColumn: decl.nameColumn))
	end 'eachDecl'
end 'seedBindings'

// ── Reference collection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ⭐⭐ **EVERY REFERENCE IS READ OFF WHAT THE RESOLUTION ALREADY PRODUCED — nothing here re-derives what a
// name means.** That is `DeadGlobalElimination`'s discipline and it is adopted for its reason: a use
// resolves local → capture → top-level, and re-deriving that order has produced a silent wrong answer
// every time something tried. So a call is a `call`/`tryCall`/`asyncCall`/`functionRef` op's own callee
// name, a stored global is a `globalAddr`'s own label, and a type is an id the type layer already interned.
//
// ⚠ Witness-table entries and function-backed enum case targets need no hand-pinned liveness roots: a
// function VALUE is emitted as a `functionRef`, so the ordinary walk below reaches them.
function collectReferences(module MaxonModule, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, moduleTypeNames TypeNameInterner)
	for func in module.functions 'eachFunc'
		if func.sourceFilePath.toString().isEmpty() 'synthesizedReaderNamesNothingAnAuthorWrote'
			continue
		end 'synthesizedReaderNamesNothingAnAuthorWrote'

		let reader = tracked.fileOf(func.sourceFilePath, signatures: signatures)
		noteSignatureTypes(func, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, moduleTypeNames: moduleTypeNames, reader: reader)
		noteBodyReferences(module, func: func, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, reader: reader)
	end 'eachFunc'

	noteCrossFileConstantReads(signatures, tracked: tracked)
	noteConstInitializerTypeNames(signatures, tracked: tracked)
	noteTopLevelInitializerCallees(signatures, tracked: tracked)
end 'collectReferences'

// A declared signature names types in the DECLARING file — its parameters, its return and its `throws`.
// That is a reference like any other: `function consumeAlias(value UnusedAlias)` is what keeps
// `UnusedAlias` alive for its own file, and `specs/unused-export.md`'s
// `error.unused-exported-typealias` is the case that pins it (the alias IS named, in-file, and is still
// E3092 because nothing OUTSIDE names it).
//
// ⛔⛔ **THE TYPES IT WALKS ARE THE *PROJECT* INTERNER'S, AND RESOLVING THEM AGAINST THE SIGNATURE INDEX'S
// WAS OPEN #56's FOURTH INSTANCE.** `ParseStaging.remapArtifact` rewrites every merged function's
// `maxonParamTypes`/`maxonReturnType` through `project.typeNames`' fold, and `TypeResolution.resolveNamedType`
// re-mints the surviving `structRef`/`interfaceRef` ids from that same table — so a signature's ids index
// `project.typeNames` and NOTHING ELSE. The index folds a SECOND, independent per-file interner: its own
// DECLARATION SWEEP's, which reads declarations and never bodies. A type named only in a BODY (an `as`
// cast target) is therefore interned by one and not the other, and every name after it sits one id apart —
// so the two tables agree only while two insertion orders coincide.
//
// ⛔ **WHAT THAT COST WAS A SUPPRESSED TRUE FINDING, NOT A FALSE ONE, AND THAT IS THE HALF NO GREEN CASE
// COULD SEE.** A misresolved id credits WHATEVER NAME occupies that slot in the other table — a name the
// reader never wrote — so a declaration nothing outside its file reaches is recorded as reached and its
// E3092/3/4 never fires. (The mirror is harmless here: the name that LOSES the credit was, by construction,
// written by that reader, and `collectFileTypeReferences` credits it from `usedTypeNames` anyway.)
// **MEASURED on this compiler's own source:** 10,568 credit events resolved to a name the project table
// does not hold there, over 426 distinct `(id, project name, index name)` triples, diverging from id 9 up.
// Correcting the resolver turned 7 reported findings into 13, and every one of the 11 declaration findings
// was TRUE — a census of the tree found no reference to any of them outside its declaring file. Adding a
// single file that declares types (`IR/Std/InlineManagedPrimitives.maxon`) had moved the divergence point
// and changed which declarations were being credited, which is how a lint whose answer depends on an
// unrelated file was noticed at all. `specs/unused-export.md`'s
// `error.unused-exported-type-when-the-two-interners-disagree` is the smallest program that shows it.
// ⇒ Every producer in this file now hands the walk THE INTERNER ITS IDS WERE MINTED AGAINST, beside the
// type. `ProgramSignatures.indexTypeNames` exists for exactly that, and its header carries #56's third
// instance (`MmRuntime.installStructRuntimeEntries`, a tuple field at id 814 read as `InstantNanos`).
function noteSignatureTypes(func IrFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, moduleTypeNames TypeNameInterner, reader AuditedFile)
	for paramType in func.maxonParamTypes 'eachParam'
		noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: paramType, typeNames: moduleTypeNames, reader: reader)
	end 'eachParam'

	match func.maxonReturnType 'ret'
		value(returned) then noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: returned, typeNames: moduleTypeNames, reader: reader)
		void then break 'ret'
	end 'ret'

	noteThrowsType(func, signatures: signatures, tracked: tracked, reader: reader)

	// ⛔⛔ **`IrFunction.valueNameIds` IS DELIBERATELY NOT READ HERE, AND THE ATTEMPT PRODUCED A WRONG
	// ANSWER.** It is the obvious source for "what named types does this body mention?" — a dense
	// per-SSA-value column of interned `TypeNameId`s. But it is dense by ValueId over a column that
	// includes slots no value in THIS function occupies, and such a slot carries a leftover tag and a
	// leftover id rather than the `UnnamedTypeId` filler its header describes.
	//
	// **MEASURED:** `function main() returns ExitCode / return entry()` — a body naming no type at all,
	// with no parameters — reports `v0 tag=named nameId=1`, and project-global id 1 was whatever alias
	// happened to intern first. So `export typealias UnusedAlias`, used only as an IN-FILE parameter
	// type, was credited with a read from `app/main.maxon` and `specs/unused-export.md`'s
	// `error.unused-exported-typealias` compiled CLEAN instead of reporting E3092. Gating on the parallel
	// `valueTags` does not cure it: the leftover slot's TAG is `named` too. Renaming the aliases moved the
	// false read to whichever one then held id 1, which is what identified it.
	//
	// ⇒ The coverage it was reaching for — "another file names this type" — is served precisely, and
	// without any interner id, by `noteQualifiedOwner` on the callee walk: a file that uses a type
	// CALLS something on it (`LocalPoint.origin()`, `p.sum()`), and the owner half of that qualified
	// callee name is the reference.
end 'noteSignatureTypes'

function noteBodyReferences(module MaxonModule, func IrFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, reader AuditedFile)
	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'eachBlock'
		let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("checkUnusedExports: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")

		for opIdx in block.opRefs 'eachOp'
			let op = try module.ops.get(opIdx) otherwise panic("checkUnusedExports: opRef {opIdx} not in module.ops")
			noteOpReferences(signatures, tracked: tracked, op: op, reader: reader)
		end 'eachOp'
	end 'eachBlock'
end 'noteBodyReferences'

// A `throws E` clause names `E` in the declaring file. Split out because a match arm is ONE statement,
// and `throwsClauseName` already answers "is there one?" by throwing rather than by a second predicate.
function noteThrowsType(func IrFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, reader AuditedFile)
	let errorName = try throwsClauseName(func.throwsTypeName) otherwise return
	noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: errorName.toByteArray(), reader: reader)
end 'noteThrowsType'

// ⭐⭐ **CALLING A FUNCTION USES ITS DECLARED ERROR TYPE, AND THE CALLER'S FILE IS WHERE THAT USE HAPPENS.**
// `try risky(9) otherwise (e)` binds `e` to `risky`'s declared error union without the caller ever writing
// the name, and it was MEASURED reporting E3092 against the very type the case exists to pass across a file
// boundary.
//
// ⛔ **THE RETURN TYPE IS NOT ASKED HERE, AND THIS HEADER CLAIMED IT WAS FOR THE WHOLE LIFE OF THE FILE**
// (found BATCH43, by the program the claim predicts: `let a = build()` then `a.n`, with `build` and its
// record declared together in another file, reported E3092 against that record and E4006 once the advice was
// taken). It is not asked because it is not this pass's to derive: a value's type matters here only when the
// reader reaches INTO it, and the lines that decide THAT are `Parser.requireFieldAccessible` and
// `Parser.emitEnumTagOf`, whose answers arrive as `FileParseArtifact.memberAccessedTypeNames`. Reading
// `returnTypeOf` as well would credit every caller of every factory with its record whether or not the caller
// ever opened one — three families of correct findings, deleted (see `collectFileTypeReferences`), plus
// `unused-export/error.unused-exported-union-nothing-outside-reaches`, whose whole subject is a file that
// receives a union value and never opens it.
function noteCalleeSignature(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, callee ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	let errorName = try throwsClauseName(signatures.throwsOf(callee)) otherwise return
	noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: errorName.toByteArray(), reader: reader)
end 'noteCalleeSignature'

function noteOpReferences(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, op MaxonOp, reader AuditedFile)
	// `direct` and `functionValue` are one answer here: both name a function this file reaches, and the
	// distinction between them is about whether a RESOLVER may rewrite the name, which this pass never does.
	if maxonOpCalleeKind(op) != MaxonCalleeKind.noCallee 'namesACallee'
		noteFunctionName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: maxonOpCalleeName(op), reader: reader)
		noteCalleeSignature(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: maxonOpCalleeName(op), reader: reader)
	end 'namesACallee'

	if maxonOpNamesAGlobalLabel(op) 'namesAStoredGlobal'
		noteGlobalLabel(signatures, tracked: tracked, label: maxonOpGlobalLabelName(op), reader: reader)
	end 'namesAStoredGlobal'
end 'noteOpReferences'

// ⭐⭐ **THE THREE ROSTERS A FILE'S NAMES SURVIVE IN — the names its parse WROTE, the types it reached a
// MEMBER of without writing anything, and the names only a TOP-LEVEL INITIALIZER spells.** None survives
// anywhere else, and the check is wrong without any of them.
//
// **WRITTEN NAMES** are the one source that survives ERASURE. A ranged typealias in a signature is `integer`
// by the time any pass sees it (MEASURED: `scoreOf(s Score)` declared in another file leaves
// `maxonParamTypes` holding `integer` with `UnnamedTypeId`), so reading declared types alone reports a
// genuinely-used `export typealias` as E3092 — a wrong answer. The parser already records this set for
// E3062, which asks the same question one scope narrower ("did this FILE use its own alias?"), so the answer
// is shared rather than re-derived.
//
// ⭐⭐ **MEMBER-ACCESSED TYPES ARE THE RESOLVER'S OWN ANSWER TO THIS PASS'S QUESTION, AND WITHOUT THEM THE
// TWO DIAGNOSTICS CONTRADICTED EACH OTHER (BATCH43).** `for it in h.items` then `it.n` requires `Item`
// VISIBLE and never spells it: the transitive walk below reaches `Holder`'s field type `ItemArray` and stops
// at the alias, so E3092 told the author to drop an `export` that E4006 then refused the access without —
// a program with no legal spelling. `Parser.requireFieldAccessible` is the line that decides that
// visibility question, so it is the line that records it; this pass ASKS the resolver instead of walking the
// type graph a second, weaker way.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THE SAME CLASS, THIRD INSTANCE: AN ENUM OR UNION REACHED THROUGH A `match` (BATCH43).** `match
// classify(42)` on another file's `union Answer` spells its CASES (`small`, `big(n)`) and never its TYPE, as
// `s.ordinal` spells a member and an interpolation hole spells nothing — so nothing written reaches
// `usedTypeNames` and the transitive walk has no field to follow. E3092 said to drop the `export`, which
// is again advice with no legal spelling. `Parser.emitEnumTagOf` — the one line that reads a tag out of
// a value of a declared enum — records it, for `requireFieldAccessible`'s reason and through its
// channel.
//
// ⚠ **IT IS NOT "EVERY TYPE STRUCTURALLY REACHABLE FROM ONE THIS FILE NAMES", AND THAT DISTINCTION IS
// MEASURED.** A reader that holds a `Crate with Item`, a `function(Payload) returns …` or a `(Elem, Integer)`
// without ever reaching INTO one compiles perfectly well once the `export` is dropped — verified on all
// three — so crediting them would delete three families of correct findings. What earns a credit is a
// visibility the resolver actually demanded.
//
// ⭐⭐ **A NAME SPELLED ONLY IN A TOP-LEVEL INITIALIZER IS INVISIBLE TO THE PARSE.** `readTopLevelBinding`
// skips an initializer's tokens wholesale — the const evaluator folds them, before any file is parsed, on a
// transient `Parser` whose artifact is discarded — so `let W = 22 as ColumnWidth` leaves NOTHING in that
// file's `usedTypeNames`. A file whose every mention of another file's alias has that shape then looks like
// no reader at all, and E3092 tells the author to drop an `export` the program needs. The evaluator records
// those names on the index instead (`ProgramSignatures.recordConstInitializerTypeName`), and they are
// credited here through the same door as the other two.
function collectFileTypeReferences(project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, userFiles FilePathArray, tracked TrackedDecls) throws CompileError
	for path in userFiles 'eachFile'
		let artifact = try queryParseOps(project, path: path)
		let reader = tracked.fileOf(path, signatures: signatures)
		noteEveryTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, roster: artifact.usedTypeNames, reader: reader)
		noteEveryTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, roster: artifact.memberAccessedTypeNames, reader: reader)
	end 'eachFile'
end 'collectFileTypeReferences'

// All three of a file's recorded name sets are credited the same way — they differ in what they MEAN, not
// in what a reference to one of their names does, so the crediting is written once.
// A walk that recorded nothing has no roster to walk — a `match` arm may not open a `for`, so the state is
// unwrapped here and the loop stays one function down.
function noteEveryTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, roster UsedTypeNameRoster, reader AuditedFile)
	match roster 'walk'
		unwritten then break 'walk'
		entries(names) then noteEachTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, names: names, reader: reader)
	end 'walk'
end 'noteEveryTypeName'

function noteEachTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, names UsedTypeNameSet, reader AuditedFile)
	for name in names 'eachName'
		noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, reader: reader)
	end 'eachName'
end 'noteEachTypeName'

// The type names only a top-level initializer spells, replayed from the log the const evaluator wrote —
// see `collectFileTypeReferences`'s header for why the parse cannot see them.
function noteConstInitializerTypeNames(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.constInitializerTypeSiteCount() 'eachSite'
		let site = signatures.constInitializerTypeSiteAt(i)
		noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: site.name, reader: tracked.fileOf(site.readerFilePath, signatures: signatures))
	end 'eachSite'
end 'noteConstInitializerTypeNames'

// See `ProgramSignatures.notedConstantValue` for why an inlined constant cannot be found in the IR at
// all.
function noteCrossFileConstantReads(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.crossFileConstantReadCount() 'eachRead'
		let read = signatures.crossFileConstantReadAt(i)
		noteBindingName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: read.name, reader: tracked.fileOf(read.readerFilePath, signatures: signatures))
	end 'eachRead'
end 'noteCrossFileConstantReads'

// ── Matching a reference to a seeded declaration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

function noteFunctionName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	noteQualifiedOwner(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: name, reader: reader)

	if let claimants = try tracked.functionIndex.get(name) 'tracked'
		noteEveryClaimant(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, claimants: claimants, reader: reader)
	end 'tracked'
end 'noteFunctionName'

// ⭐ **A CALL TO `Owner.member` IS A REFERENCE TO `Owner`.** This is how one file names another file's
// TYPE in practice — `LocalPoint.origin()`, `p.sum()`, `Status.fromRawValue(…)` — and it is read off the
// callee name the resolution already produced, so it needs no interner id and cannot collide the way
// `IrFunction.valueNameIds` did (see `noteSignatureTypes`). A callee whose owner half is not a tracked
// type simply matches nothing: a namespace-qualified free function (`api.helper`) resolves against the
// FUNCTION index above, not this one.
function noteQualifiedOwner(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, callee ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	match splitQualifiedName(callee) 'split'
		notQualified then return
		parts(owner, _) then noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: owner, reader: reader)
	end 'split'
end 'noteQualifiedOwner'

// ⭐⭐ **USING A TYPE USES THE TYPES IT IS MADE OF, AND WITHOUT THAT THE CHECK REPORTS A WRONG ANSWER.**
// A file can depend on a type without ever writing its name: `let c = Gate.make().c` names `Gate` and
// consumes a `Color`, and `try f() otherwise …` catches a `Woe` its file never spells. MEASURED — those
// two shapes were 9 of the corpus's failures, every one of them a spec whose SUBJECT is that the
// cross-file reference works.
function noteTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	if not tracked.creditsTypeNameFirst(name, reader: reader) 'alreadyCredited'
		return
	end 'alreadyCredited'

	if let claimants = try tracked.typeIndex.get(name) 'tracked'
		noteEveryClaimant(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, claimants: claimants, reader: reader)
	end 'tracked'

	// A type this pass does not TRACK is still walked through: a file-private struct may hold a field of
	// an exported type, and a reader that reaches the one reaches the other.
	noteStructFieldTypes(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, reader: reader)
	noteEnumPayloadTypes(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, reader: reader)
end 'noteTypeName'

function noteStructFieldTypes(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	match signatures.structFor(name, readerFilePath: reader.path) 'lookup'
		undeclared then return

		// A layout the SIGNATURE INDEX built, so its field-type ids are the index's own — see
		// `noteSignatureTypes` for what resolving them anywhere else costs.
		declared(layout) then noteComponentTypes(signatures, tracked: tracked, types: layout.fieldTypes, typeNames: signatures.indexTypeNames(), reader: reader)
	end 'lookup'
end 'noteStructFieldTypes'

function noteEnumPayloadTypes(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	match signatures.enumFor(name, readerFilePath: reader.path) 'lookup'
		undeclared then return
		declared(layout) then noteEveryPayloadType(signatures, tracked: tracked, layout: layout, reader: reader)
	end 'lookup'
end 'noteEnumPayloadTypes'

function noteEveryPayloadType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, layout EnumLayout, reader AuditedFile)
	// ⭐⭐ **A STRUCT-BACKED UNION'S BACKING IS A TYPE IT IS MADE OF, AND IT IS THE ONE A READER NEVER
	// SPELLS.** `op.rawValue.isMemory` reaches `TargetOpMeta` through `TargetOp` and names it nowhere, so
	// the reader file's `usedTypeNames` cannot carry it and this walk was the only route left. Exactly the
	// argument the payload loop below makes — *"using a type uses the types it is made of"* — for the half
	// of an enum layout that is not a payload.
	if not layout.backingStructName.isEmpty() 'structBacked'
		noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: layout.backingStructName, reader: reader)
	end 'structBacked'

	// The index's own layout again — `noteStructFieldTypes`' interner, for its reason. Taken once rather
	// than per field: it is a handle to the index's table, and this is the innermost loop of the walk.
	let payloadTypeNames = signatures.indexTypeNames()

	for payloadFields in layout.casePayloads 'eachCase'
		for field in payloadFields 'eachField'
			noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: field.declaredType, typeNames: payloadTypeNames, reader: reader)
		end 'eachField'
	end 'eachCase'
end 'noteEveryPayloadType'

function noteComponentTypes(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, types MaxonTypeArray, typeNames TypeNameInterner, reader AuditedFile)
	for fieldType in types 'eachField'
		noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: fieldType, typeNames: typeNames, reader: reader)
	end 'eachField'
end 'noteComponentTypes'

// ⛔ **`typeNameIdOf` IS NOT A NAME-ID GETTER FOR EVERY ARM, AND USING IT AS ONE CONFLATES TWO ID
// SPACES.** Its `typeParameter` and `genericInstance` arms return a type-parameter DIGEST and a
// `GenericInstanceId` — both ride the same column so the value round-trips, but neither indexes the type
// NAME interner. Resolving one through `typeNameOf` asks the wrong table and answers with whatever name
// happens to occupy that slot, which is the same shape of defect `IrFunction.valueNameIds` produced.
//
// ⭐ And a generic instance's TYPE ARGUMENTS are references in their own right: `Array with Item` names
// `Item`, and nothing else in this walk would ever reach it.
//
// ⭐⭐ **`typeNames` IS WHICH NAME TABLE THE NAME-BEARING ARMS INDEX, AND IT IS A PARAMETER BECAUSE THE
// CALLERS ARE IN TWO DIFFERENT SPACES.** A signature's types are the PROJECT interner's and a layout's are
// the SIGNATURE INDEX's — see `noteSignatureTypes` for the measurement and for what a crossed pair costs.
// It rides beside the type it resolves rather than being derived from `signatures`, which is the only
// honest way for a walk with two entrances to say which space it was entered from.
// (The two id-space arms below are unaffected: a `typeParameter`'s digest and a `GenericInstanceId` are
// whole-program payloads, interner-independent by construction — `remapMaxonType` passes both through a
// merge unchanged for exactly that reason.)
function noteComponentType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, type MaxonType, typeNames TypeNameInterner, reader AuditedFile)
	match type 'type'
		named(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, typeNames: typeNames, reader: reader)
		structRef(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, typeNames: typeNames, reader: reader)
		interfaceRef(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, typeNames: typeNames, reader: reader)
		function(id) then noteComponentTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, nameId: id, typeNames: typeNames, reader: reader)
		genericInstance(id) then noteInstanceArgs(signatures, tracked: tracked, id: id, reader: reader)

		// A type PARAMETER's id is a digest, not a name, and the parameter itself names no declaration.
		typeParameter then return
		boolean or
			integer or
			float then return
		exitCode or
			unresolved then return
		string then return
		character then return
		cstring then return
	end 'type'
end 'noteComponentType'

// ⚠ **A SUBSTITUTED INSTANCE ARGUMENT IS INTERNED IN THE INDEX**, whichever space the instance reference
// itself arrived from — `ProgramSignatures.indexSpaceTypeName` is the door that says so, and its own panic
// message is #56's third instance. So this hop RE-STATES the interner rather than forwarding its caller's.
function noteInstanceArgs(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, id GenericInstanceId, reader AuditedFile)
	let argTypeNames = signatures.indexTypeNames()

	for position in 0 upto signatures.genericInstanceArgCount(id) 'eachArg'
		noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: signatures.substitutedInstanceArg(id, position: position), typeNames: argTypeNames, reader: reader)
	end 'eachArg'
end 'noteInstanceArgs'

function noteComponentTypeName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, nameId TypeNameId, typeNames TypeNameInterner, reader AuditedFile)
	if nameId == UnnamedTypeId 'namesNothing'
		return
	end 'namesNothing'

	let componentName = try typeNames.nameOf(nameId) otherwise return
	noteTypeName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: componentName, reader: reader)
end 'noteComponentTypeName'

function noteBindingName(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	noteQualifiedOwner(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: name, reader: reader)

	if let claimants = try tracked.bindingIndex.get(name) 'tracked'
		noteEveryClaimant(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: name, claimants: claimants, reader: reader)
	end 'tracked'
end 'noteBindingName'

// A stored global is reached by its `.data` LABEL, which is what the op carries; the seed is keyed by
// source name. The arena holds both, so the label is translated here rather than the seed being keyed by
// something a `let` does not have (an immutable binding has no label at all — see `TopLevelDecl.dataLabel`).
// A label no declaration owns names nothing this pass tracks — the honest answer for a `.data` slot the
// compiler minted for itself, and the same answer the scan's fall-through gave.
function noteGlobalLabel(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, label ByteArray, reader AuditedFile)
	let index = try tracked.globalLabels.get(label) otherwise return
	let decl = signatures.declAt(index)
	noteBindingName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: decl.name, reader: reader)
	noteSlotType(signatures, tracked: tracked, index: index, reader: reader)
end 'noteGlobalLabel'

// ⭐⭐ **THE CLASSIFICATION RULE, AND ITS ONE DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM WHAT `module` MEANS.** A reader in
// the SAME DIRECTORY as the declaration counts as OUTSIDE its module subtree, even though
// `Visibility.module` would make the declaration visible to it. It is not an oversight: without it,
// every flat two-file program would be told to downgrade its `export`s to `module`, which is advice
// about a program's directory layout rather than about its visibility. Only a STRICTLY NESTED reader
// keeps a declaration downgradable — which is why the equality case is excluded here rather than left
// to `moduleDirectoryContains`, whose own answer includes it.
function noteRead(tracked TrackedDecls, index TrackedDeclIndex, reader AuditedFile)
	var decl = tracked.at(index)

	// Both bits only ever widen, so a declaration already read from outside its subtree has nothing left to learn.
	if decl.sawOutsideModule or decl.declFile.index == reader.index 'nothingToWidenOrItsOwnFile'
		return
	end 'nothingToWidenOrItsOwnFile'

	// ⭐⭐ **A LIBRARY FILE CANNOT NAME AN AUTHOR'S DECLARATION — A CREDIT THAT SAYS OTHERWISE IS A
	// MONOMORPH'S SIGNATURE, NOT A REFERENCE.** `stdlib/` is compiled with no knowledge whatever of user
	// code, so no line in it can mention `type Item`; what the walk actually met is `ArrayIterator.create`
	// INSTANTIATED over the author's element type, whose `sourceFilePath` is `stdlib/Array.maxon` because
	// that is where its body was written. The instantiation was demanded by an author's file, and that file
	// is credited on its own wherever it genuinely reaches the type.
	//
	// ⛔ **CREDITING ONE SUPPRESSES TRUE FINDINGS, UNPREDICTABLY.** Whether a monomorphized iterator's
	// signature mentions the author's `Item` at all turns on what the reading file happens to declare, so two
	// programs differing in nothing else answer differently about one `export type Item`. It also makes the
	// E3093 half unfalsifiable: every route by which an outside file reaches a container's ELEMENT type runs
	// through a library generic.
	//
	// ⚠ **ONE DIRECTION ONLY.** A library file reading a LIBRARY declaration is an ordinary reference, and it
	// is what keeps `stdlib/String.maxon`'s `module` declarations audited (see this file's header).
	if reader.isLibrary and not decl.declFile.isLibrary 'aLibraryBodyNamedNothingTheAuthorWrote'
		return
	end 'aLibraryBodyNamedNothingTheAuthorWrote'

	decl.sawOutsideFile = true

	let declModuleDirectory = decl.declFile.moduleDirectory
	let strictlyNested = moduleDirectoryContains(declModuleDirectory, inner: reader.moduleDirectory) and not declModuleDirectory.equals(reader.moduleDirectory)

	if not strictlyNested 'outsideTheSubtree'
		decl.sawOutsideModule = true
	end 'outsideTheSubtree'

	try tracked.entries.set(index, value: decl) otherwise panic("checkUnusedExports: entries.set OOB at {index} — the index came from this seed")
end 'noteRead'

// ── Emission ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

typealias DemandedTierMap = Map with (ByteArray, Visibility)

// The widest tier any REACHED signature demands of each type name. A demand is `checkSignatureVisibility`'s
// record that some function's signature names the type and so needs it at the tier E3167 judges that
// function at; it is reached when the demanding function is itself referenced from outside the type's
// declaring file, since a function nothing outside reaches is an `export` the author may drop, and
// crediting the type off it would
// suppress the finding that says so.
//
// `Visibility.file` is the "no reached demand" value and no demand can carry it — the pass never judges a
// file-private function.
function reachedSignatureDemands(project Project, tracked TrackedDecls) returns DemandedTierMap
	var demanded = DemandedTierMap.create()

	for demand in project.signatureTypeDemands 'eachDemand'
		if tierIsAtLeastAsVisible(try demanded.get(demand.typeName) otherwise Visibility.file, floor: demand.demandingTier) 'aWiderDemandIsAlreadyHeld'
			continue
		end 'aWiderDemandIsAlreadyHeld'

		if not demandIsReached(tracked, demand: demand) 'itsDemanderIsReachedInItsOwnFileAlone'
			continue
		end 'itsDemanderIsReachedInItsOwnFileAlone'

		demanded.upsert(demand.typeName, value: demand.demandingTier)
	end 'eachDemand'

	return demanded
end 'reachedSignatureDemands'

function demandIsReached(tracked TrackedDecls, demand SignatureTypeDemand) returns bool
	match splitQualifiedName(demand.demandingFunction) 'split'
		notQualified then return reachedFromOutsideItsFile(tracked.functionIndex, tracked: tracked, name: demand.demandingFunction)
		parts(owner, _) then return memberDemandIsReached(tracked, demand: demand, owner: owner)
	end 'split'
end 'demandIsReached'

// A method's OWNER TYPE stands in for it: this audit records no reference against a method at all — the
// type owns the finding — so asking the member's own reach would answer false for every member demand and
// credit nothing. A member the seed does track answers for itself.
function memberDemandIsReached(tracked TrackedDecls, demand SignatureTypeDemand, owner ByteArray) returns bool
	if owner.equals(demand.typeName) 'aMemberCannotWidenItsOwnType'
		return false
	end 'aMemberCannotWidenItsOwnType'

	if tracked.functionIndex.contains(demand.demandingFunction) 'theMemberIsAuditedItself'
		return reachedFromOutsideItsFile(tracked.functionIndex, tracked: tracked, name: demand.demandingFunction)
	end 'theMemberIsAuditedItself'

	return reachedFromOutsideItsFile(tracked.typeIndex, tracked: tracked, name: owner)
end 'memberDemandIsReached'

function reachedFromOutsideItsFile(index TrackedDeclIndexMap, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray) returns bool
	// A name the seed never tracked — a `public` declaration, an entry point, a task — is one whose reach
	// this pass does not measure, so its demand stands. Answering true can only credit the type and so
	// suppress a finding; it never invents one.
	let claimants = try index.get(name) otherwise return true

	for at in claimants 'eachClaimant'
		if tracked.at(at).sawOutsideFile 'reachedFromOutside'
			return true
		end 'reachedFromOutside'
	end 'eachClaimant'

	return false
end 'reachedFromOutsideItsFile'

// In DECLARATION order, which is the order the seed was built in — see `TrackedDecls`.
//
// ⛔ The RUNTIME tier's declarations are dropped HERE rather than at seed time, and a set lookup rather
// than a path probe, for the reason `LibrarySourcePathSet` states: this runs per tracked DECLARATION,
// not per file, and the answer was already computed once per file by `splitSourcePaths`. See this
// file's header for why the tier is exempt at all.
function emitDiagnostics(project Project, tracked TrackedDecls, runtimeFiles LibrarySourcePathSet, demanded DemandedTierMap)
	for i in 0 upto tracked.entries.count() 'eachTracked'
		let decl = tracked.at(i)

		if runtimeFiles.contains(decl.declFile.pathText) 'theRuntimeTiersOwn'
			continue
		end 'theRuntimeTiersOwn'

		emitOne(project, decl: decl, demandedTier: demandedTierOf(decl, demanded: demanded))
	end 'eachTracked'
end 'emitDiagnostics'

function demandedTierOf(decl TrackedDecl, demanded DemandedTierMap) returns Visibility
	if decl.kind != TrackedDeclKind.trackedType 'onlyATypeIsNamedByASignature'
		return Visibility.file
	end 'onlyATypeIsNamedByASignature'

	return try demanded.get(decl.key) otherwise Visibility.file
end 'demandedTierOf'

function emitOne(project Project, decl TrackedDecl, demandedTier Visibility)
	match decl.visibility 'tier'
		file then panic("checkUnusedExports: a `file` declaration reached emit ({decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}') — `tierIsAudited` filters it at seed time")
		public then panic("checkUnusedExports: a `public` declaration reached emit ({decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}') — `tierIsAudited` filters it at seed time, which is the whole of the exemption")
		module then emitForModuleTier(project, decl: decl, demandedTier: demandedTier)
		global then emitForGlobalTier(project, decl: decl, demandedTier: demandedTier)
	end 'tier'
end 'emitOne'

function emitForModuleTier(project Project, decl TrackedDecl, demandedTier Visibility)
	if tierIsAtLeastAsVisible(demandedTier, floor: Visibility.module) 'aReachedSignatureAsksForThisTier'
		return
	end 'aReachedSignatureAsksForThisTier'

	if not decl.sawOutsideFile 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'
		reportPositioned(project, code: ErrorCode.semanticUnusedModuleSymbol, message: "module {decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}' is never referenced outside its declaring file", line: decl.nameLine, column: decl.nameColumn, filePath: decl.declFile.path)
	end 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'
end 'emitForModuleTier'

// The demand excuses each arm on its own terms, not the declaration as a whole: a `module` demand answers
// "nothing outside names it" but leaves "`module` would do" true and worth saying, so only a program-wide
// demand silences both arms.
function emitForGlobalTier(project Project, decl TrackedDecl, demandedTier Visibility)
	if isProgramWideTier(demandedTier) 'aReachedSignatureAsksForThisTier'
		return
	end 'aReachedSignatureAsksForThisTier'

	if not decl.sawOutsideFile and demandedTier == Visibility.file 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'
		reportPositioned(project, code: ErrorCode.semanticUnusedExportedSymbol, message: "exported {decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}' is never referenced outside its declaring file", line: decl.nameLine, column: decl.nameColumn, filePath: decl.declFile.path)
		return
	end 'nothingOutsideNamesIt'

	if not decl.sawOutsideModule 'onlyItsOwnSubtreeNamesIt'
		reportPositioned(project, code: ErrorCode.semanticExportableAsModule, message: "exported {decl.noun} '{decl.displayName}' is only referenced inside its declaring module subtree; consider 'module' visibility", line: decl.nameLine, column: decl.nameColumn, filePath: decl.declFile.path)
	end 'onlyItsOwnSubtreeNamesIt'
end 'emitForGlobalTier'

// ⭐ **A TOP-LEVEL INITIALIZER'S CALLS, ATTRIBUTED TO THE FILE THAT WROTE THEM.** `var a = Outer.build()`
// is lowered into the synthesized `__module_init`, whose `sourceFilePath` is empty — so the body walk
// skips it and the call is invisible. Asked per DECLARATION instead, which is what carries the declaring
// file, rather than off `globalInitCallees()`, whose flat list has lost it. MEASURED on
// `top-level-factory-globals/factory-returning-a-record-declared-in-another-file`.
function noteTopLevelInitializerCallees(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls)
	for i in 0 upto signatures.topLevelDeclCount() 'eachDecl'
		let decl = signatures.declAt(i)
		noteOneInitializersCallees(signatures, tracked: tracked, decl: decl)
	end 'eachDecl'
end 'noteTopLevelInitializerCallees'

function noteOneInitializersCallees(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, decl TopLevelDecl)
	match signatures.declInitializerCall(decl) 'initializer'
		none then return
		calls(callees) then noteEveryInitializerCallee(signatures, tracked: tracked, callees: callees, reader: tracked.fileOf(decl.declFilePath, signatures: signatures))
	end 'initializer'
end 'noteOneInitializersCallees'

function noteEveryInitializerCallee(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, callees ByteArrayArray, reader AuditedFile)
	for callee in callees 'eachCallee'
		noteFunctionName(signatures, tracked: tracked, name: callee, reader: reader)
		noteCalleeSignature(signatures, tracked: tracked, callee: callee, reader: reader)
	end 'eachCallee'
end 'noteEveryInitializerCallee'

// Every declaration wearing the referenced name — see `TrackedDeclIndexMap` for why there can be more
// than one and why crediting all of them is the safe direction.
//
// ⛔ **EXCEPT A DECLARATION THIS READER DOES NOT MEAN BY THE NAME, WHICH IS THE ONE WAY "CREDIT THEM ALL"
// IS NOT SAFE.** Crediting a spare claimant only ever SUPPRESSES a warning, so the direction is right for
// two declarations a reader genuinely could mean — but a cross-KIND contested name is two declarations
// that CANNOT both be meant, and crediting the wrong one makes this audit's answer depend on an unrelated
// file's spelling. MEASURED, one program twice: with `a.maxon`'s file-private alias named `Other`,
// `b.maxon`'s `export union Container` earned `E3092: exported type 'Container' is never referenced
// outside its declaring file`; with the alias named `Container`, `a.maxon`'s uses of its OWN alias were
// counted as references to that union and **the diagnostic vanished**.
//
// ⚠ It is the CONTEST that is asked and not visibility: a name only one kind holds is credited exactly as
// before, which is every name in every program in the corpus.
function noteEveryClaimant(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, name ByteArray, claimants TrackedDeclIndexArray, reader AuditedFile)
	if signatures.crossKindContested(name) and signatures.contestGivesThisReaderAScalar(name, readerFilePath: reader.path) 'thisReaderMeansTheAlias'
		return
	end 'thisReaderMeansTheAlias'

	for at in claimants 'eachClaimant'
		noteRead(tracked, index: at, reader: reader)
	end 'eachClaimant'
end 'noteEveryClaimant'

// ⭐ **REFERENCING A BINDING USES ITS TYPE** — see `ProgramSignatures.globalSlotType` for the measurement.
// The slot type is walked with the same transitive rules a field type is, so naming `db` reaches
// `Database`, the `EntryMap` it holds and the `Entry` inside that.
function noteSlotType(signatures ProgramSignatures, tracked TrackedDecls, index TopLevelDeclIndex, reader AuditedFile)
	match signatures.globalSlotType(index) 'slot'
		notFound then return

		// `globalSlotType` ADOPTS the slot's type into the index's own interner — that is the whole reason
		// it exists as its own door rather than taking a table — so the walk is told exactly that.
		found(_, valueType, _, _) then noteComponentType(signatures, tracked: tracked, type: valueType, typeNames: signatures.indexTypeNames(), reader: reader)
	end 'slot'
end 'noteSlotType'
